        <obo:IAO_0000115>Voltammetry applies a constant and-or varying potential at an electrode&apos;s surface and measures the resulting current with a three electrode system. Polarometry is a subclass of voltammetry. Amperometry is also a subclass of voltammetry.</obo:IAO_0000115>
