    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://semanticlookup.zbmed.de/km/fskxo/FSKXO_0000017811">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://semanticlookup.zbmed.de/km/fskxo/FSKXO_0000017800"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Valid JSON Object
JSON objects are surrounded by curly braces {}.written in key/value pairs.Keys must be strings, and values must be a valid data type 
Keys and values are separated by a colon. Each key/value pair is separated by a comma.
{ &quot;name&quot;:&quot;John&quot;, &quot;age&quot;:30, &quot;car&quot;:null }</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://semanticlookup.zbmed.de/km/fskxo"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Object</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://semanticlookup.zbmed.de/km/fskxo/FSKXO_0000017812 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://semanticlookup.zbmed.de/km/fskxo/FSKXO_0000017812">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://semanticlookup.zbmed.de/km/fskxo/FSKXO_0000017800"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The quality measures can be defined as an object (JSON) with keys &apos;SSE&apos;, &apos;MSE&apos;, &apos;RMSE&apos;, &apos;Rsquared&apos;, &apos;AIC&apos;, &apos;BIC&apos; and &apos;sensitivy_analysis&apos;.
The &apos;sensitivity analysis&apos; property is of type Other while the rest of properties are Double.
Example: {&apos;SSE&apos;: 0, &apos;MSE&apos;: 0, &apos;RMSE&apos;: 0, &apos;AIC&apos;: 0, &apos;BIC&apos;: 0, &apos;sensitivity_analysis&apos;: &apos;text&apos; }                  </obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://semanticlookup.zbmed.de/km/fskxo"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Quality measures</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


